<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<jmeterTestPlan version="1.2" properties="5.0" jmeter="5.6.3">
  <hashTree>
    <TestPlan guiclass="TestPlanGui" testclass="TestPlan" testname="CMS V2 Lifecycle Functional" enabled="true">
      <stringProp name="TestPlan.comments">CMS V2 lifecycle functional coverage.
Runner: stock JMeter 5.6.3 with Java 21, or Java 25 with all Groovy libraries updated to 3.0.25.
CMS Core: Java 25 / Spring Boot 4. Use run_functional.ps1 for runtime selection and compilation checks.

Carries the CMS_V2_LIFECYCLE_COVERAGE_GAPS.md families that are not already proved by
CMS_V2_INSTITUTION_TO_REPLACEMENT_VIRTUAL.jmx or CMS_V2_INSTITUTION_TO_REPLACEMENT_STEP_BY_STEP.jmx, and that a
JMeter client can establish through the public API plus disposable-database fixtures.

Thread group 00 builds the shared institution, 6- and 8-digit BINs, ranges, card designs,
vendor/batch fixtures, virtual and physical-mode products (with personalisation,
technology and CVM profiles), HSM keys, then customer/account/address fixtures via
customer-service V2 (plus JDBC restriction snapshots, activation policy and draft-policy
activations), then publishes the identifiers as JMeter properties. Groups 10-26 cover
the original gap families. Groups
27-40 add review feedback for product configuration depth, issuance modes, replacement
and PIN boundaries, canonical lifecycle commands, institution/BIN/HSM depth, broader
idempotency, envelope and pagination contracts, outbox ops, and permission/resilience
catalogues. Accounting (13), performance (16) and database migration (17) stay out of
this plan.

Every later group hydrates shared properties, authenticates, and creates only the card
fixtures it needs. Groups run in order and continue after a failed assertion, so one
broken rule does not hide the rest of the matrix.

Families needing fault injection, a controllable clock, process restarts, restricted
permission clients or Switch authorization traffic are documented in
CMS_V2_LIFECYCLE_FUNCTIONAL.md rather than simulated here.

Requires ALLOW_TEST_FIXTURES=true against a disposable database, customer-service V2
reachable at CUSTOMER_SERVICE_HOST:CUSTOMER_SERVICE_PORT, and the embossing service
reachable at EMBOSSING_HOST:EMBOSSING_PORT (default localhost:8089). Group 28 calls the
embossing personalisation batch and file read APIs. Set WAIT_FOR_SWITCH_SYNC=true when
Switch is running.</stringProp>
      <boolProp name="TestPlan.functional_mode">true</boolProp>
      <boolProp name="TestPlan.serialize_threadgroups">true</boolProp>
